\section{Entanglement Classes and the Quark--Lepton Division}
\label{sec:entanglement-classes}

The previous section left us with the gauge group $G_{\mathrm{SM}}$ acting on the split
$\mathbb{O} \cong \mathbb{C} \oplus \mathbb{C}^3$ once a complex direction is fixed
(Proposition~\ref{prop:gsm}), and with the entanglement-sensitivity of the octonionic Hopf map
as the hinge of any physical reading. We now cash that in. The two inequivalent classes of
genuinely tripartite three-qubit entanglement map onto the two summands of the split, so that the
division of fermions into quarks and leptons follows from the entanglement \emph{type} of the
three-qubit state rather than being assigned by hand.

It should be said at once what is and is not new here. The identification of the $\mathbb{C}$
summand with a colour singlet and the $\mathbb{C}^3$ summand with a colour triplet --- leptons and
quarks respectively --- is already in the literature at the level of representations, both in
Krasnov's spinorial treatment \autocite{krasnov2021so9} and, in a form especially close to ours,
in Szangolies's recent paper \autocite{szangolies2025standardmodel}. What the present section adds
is that the \emph{SLOCC class} of the three-qubit state selects which summand it can occupy:
the genuinely tripartite GHZ class is confined to $\mathbb{C}^3$, while the distributed W class
generically reaches $\mathbb{C}$. The assignment becomes a theorem about entanglement, and the
relationship to Szangolies's work is one of convergence, set out in
\S\ref{sec:entanglement-szangolies}.

\subsection{The two classes of tripartite entanglement}

Three qubits admit exactly two inequivalent classes of genuinely tripartite entanglement under
stochastic local operations and classical communication: the GHZ class and the W class
\autocite{durvidalcirac2000three}. They are distinguished by every reasonable invariant. The
three-tangle is maximal on GHZ and identically zero on W \autocite{coffmankunduwootters2000distributed};
tracing out one qubit of a GHZ state leaves the remaining pair separable, whereas the same
operation on a W state leaves them entangled. Coecke and Kissinger sharpened the distinction into
an algebraic one: GHZ-class states induce a \emph{special} commutative Frobenius algebra and
W-class states an \emph{anti-special} one, the difference being purely topological --- whether a
certain compose--decompose loop is connected or annihilates \autocite{coeckekissinger2010compositional}.
The two Frobenius structures are the primitives of a graphical calculus expressive enough to
generate arbitrary $N$-qubit states, so that no genuinely new entanglement primitive appears beyond
three qubits. This dovetails with the termination established in the previous section: the
division-algebra ladder closes at $\mathbb{O}$ (Proposition~\ref{prop:termination}), and the
entanglement alphabet closes at the same point.

\subsection{The map into the octonion algebra}

We use the identification, set out in full in the companion derivations, of a three-qubit state
$\psi \in \mathbb{C}^8$ with a pair of octonions $(o_1, o_2) \in \mathbb{O}^2$ obtained by splitting
on the first qubit under the Cayley--Dickson correspondence, together with the $\mathbb{O}$-valued
part of the octonionic Hopf map $\mathbf{h} = o_1 \bar{o}_2$. Fixing the preferred complex direction
$e_1$ --- the computability split, the same singling-out discussed in \S\ref{sec:fanout-direction}
--- gives $\mathbb{O} \cong \mathbb{C} \oplus \mathbb{C}^3$, with $\mathbb{C} = \{e_0, e_1\}$ and
$\mathbb{C}^3 = \{e_2,\dots,e_7\}$ carrying the $\mathbf{3} \oplus \bar{\mathbf{3}}$ of the colour
$SU(3) \subset G_2$. The whole of the analysis rests on a single identity.

\begin{lemma}[$\mathbb{C}$-projection is a Hermitian inner product]\label{lem:cproj}
With the Cayley--Dickson identification above, the projection of $\mathbf{h}$ onto the
$\mathbb{C} = \{e_0, e_1\}$ summand satisfies
\[
  \pi_{\mathbb{C}}(\mathbf{h}) \;=\; \overline{\langle o_1, o_2\rangle_{\mathbb{C}^4}},
\]
where $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\mathbb{C}^4}$ is the standard Hermitian inner product on the
$\mathbb{C}^4$ that $\psi$'s first-qubit branches inhabit. Hence $\pi_{\mathbb{C}}(\mathbf{h}) = 0$
if and only if the two branches $o_1, o_2$ are $\mathbb{C}^4$-orthogonal.
\end{lemma}

The lemma is proved by checking on basis pairs and using the Fano multiplication rules; the
$\mathbb{C}$-component collects exactly the four index pairs $\{0,1\},\{2,3\},\{4,5\},\{6,7\}$ that
constitute the Hermitian inner product with $e_1$ as the imaginary unit
\autocite{baez2002octonions}. The composition-algebra identity $|\mathbf{h}|^2 = |o_1|^2|o_2|^2$,
which holds on $\mathbb{O}$ and on no larger Cayley--Dickson algebra, makes the resulting
\emph{$\mathbb{C}$-fraction} $C_{\mathrm{frac}}(\psi) = |\pi_{\mathbb{C}}(\mathbf{h})|^2/|\mathbf{h}|^2$
a well-defined local invariant. It is worth noting that $e_1$ is not merely a convenient choice:
it is the unique direction along which the relevant subalgebra is commutative, which is precisely
what makes the cancellation in the next proposition go through, and which ties the selection of the
direction back to the measurement argument of \S\ref{sec:fanout-direction}.

\subsection{GHZ states are confined to the colour sector}

\begin{proposition}[GHZ confinement]\label{prop:ghz}
Let $\psi$ lie in the SLOCC orbit of $\lvert\mathrm{GHZ}\rangle = (\lvert000\rangle + \lvert111\rangle)/\sqrt2$
under the full local unitary group $SU(2)^3$. Then $\pi_{\mathbb{C}}(\mathbf{h}(\psi)) = 0$ identically,
so the Hopf image lies entirely in the colour-triplet sector $\mathbb{C}^3 = \mathbf{3} \oplus \bar{\mathbf{3}}$.
The statement holds symmetrically under each of the three choices of qubit to split on. Conversely,
among genuinely tripartite states, vanishing $\mathbb{C}$-projection under every split characterises
the GHZ class.
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
By Lemma~\ref{lem:cproj} it suffices to show $\langle o_1, o_2\rangle_{\mathbb{C}^4} = 0$ for every
local-unitary image. The bare GHZ state has orthogonal branches of \emph{equal} norm
($\rho_k = \tfrac12\mathbb{I}$ for every $k$). The internal unitaries $U_2 \otimes U_3$ preserve both
orthogonality and equal norms; the first-qubit unitary $U_1 = \begin{psmallmatrix} a & b \\ -\bar b & \bar a\end{psmallmatrix}$
mixes the branches, and the inner product evaluates to
$-\bar a \bar b \cdot \tfrac12 + \bar b \bar a \cdot \tfrac12 = 0$, the cancellation holding because
multiplication in $\mathbb{C}$ is commutative. The full proof and the converse are given in Paper~2.
\end{proof}

The cancellation is exact, and numerically the $\mathbb{C}$-fraction over $2\times10^4$ random
$SU(2)^3$ samples sits at machine zero ($<10^{-15}$) under all three splits. Two consequences follow,
both \emph{proved} rather than conjectured. First, confinement is topological: since the
$\mathbb{C}$-projection is continuous and identically zero on the GHZ stratum but generically nonzero
on the W stratum, it is a discrete invariant of the SLOCC class, and no continuous parameter can
carry a colour triplet out of $\mathbb{C}^3$ into the lepton sector --- confinement is structural,
not dynamical. Second, the QCD vacuum angle vanishes: the GHZ image carries no oriented pairwise
linking structure capable of orienting the $\theta\,\mathrm{Tr}(G\wedge G)$ term, so $\theta_{\mathrm{QCD}} = 0$
is forced and no Peccei--Quinn axion is admitted. The identification therefore reads GHZ $\leftrightarrow$
colour triplet $\leftrightarrow$ quark, with the colour-triplet $\mathbb{C}^3$ occupying the short-root
coset of $G_2$ in the corrected assignment of \S\ref{sec:hopf-justification}.

\subsection{W states reach the lepton sector and carry the weak doublet}

\begin{proposition}[W accessibility]\label{prop:w-access}
For $\psi$ in the SLOCC orbit of $\lvert\mathrm{W}\rangle = (\lvert001\rangle + \lvert010\rangle + \lvert100\rangle)/\sqrt3$,
the Hopf image has generically nonzero $\mathbb{C}$-projection; it vanishes only on a measure-zero
subset of $SU(2)^3$, and $\sup_{U_1} C_{\mathrm{frac}} = \tfrac19$.
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
The W branches are orthogonal but of \emph{unequal} norm, $\lvert o_1\rvert^2 = \tfrac23$,
$\lvert o_2\rvert^2 = \tfrac13$ (equivalently $\rho_k$ has spectrum $(\tfrac23,\tfrac13)$). The same
mixing computation now gives $\langle o_1, o_2\rangle_{\mathbb{C}^4} = \bar a\bar b\,(-\tfrac23 + \tfrac13)
= -\tfrac13\,\bar a\bar b$, which vanishes only when $U_1$ is diagonal or anti-diagonal. The supremum
follows from maximising the exact expression $C_{\mathrm{frac}} = p(1-p)/[(1+p)(2-p)]$ at $p = \tfrac12$.
\end{proof}

The contrast with GHZ is entirely in the branch norms: equal norms force the cancellation, unequal
norms leave a residue. The same $(\tfrac23,\tfrac13)$ spectrum underwrites the weak-doublet content.

\begin{proposition}[W carries the $SU(2)_L$ doublet]\label{prop:w-doublet}
For any W-class state, each single-qubit reduced state $\rho_k$ is supported on a two-dimensional
subspace carrying the fundamental representation of $SU(2)$, with
$\rho_k = \tfrac13\mathbb{I} + \tfrac13\bigl(\lvert v_1\rangle\langle v_1\rvert - \lvert v_2\rangle\langle v_2\rvert\bigr)$:
an $SU(2)$-invariant singlet background of weight $\tfrac13$ plus a traceless preferred-direction
component that transforms as a doublet. The decomposition is symmetric across all three qubits.
\end{proposition}

The proof is immediate from the spectrum and the fact that the only faithful two-dimensional
representation of $SU(2)$ is the fundamental; tracing W over a single qubit returns
$\tfrac23\lvert\Psi^+\rangle\langle\Psi^+\rvert + \tfrac13\lvert00\rangle\langle00\rvert$, a genuine
Bell pair weighted against a separable tail, which is the pairwise shadow of the doublet. The W
class therefore reads W $\leftrightarrow$ colour singlet $\leftrightarrow$ lepton, organised into
weak-isospin doublets. Which of the two quaternionic actions $SU(2)_L$ (left multiplication) or
$SU(2)_R$ (right multiplication) becomes physical weak isospin is inherited from the third qubit
through the same computability split; we treat that selection as \emph{structural} and defer its
full formulation.

\subsection{The dictionary}

Collecting the strands, the correspondence between entanglement structure and the matter and gauge
content of the Standard Model reads as follows, with the gauge rows established in
\S\ref{sec:hopf-justification} and the fermion rows the content of Propositions~\ref{prop:ghz}--\ref{prop:w-doublet}.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{llll}
\hline
Entanglement & Division algebra & Hopf fibration & Standard Model \\
\hline
separable & $\mathbb{C}$ & $S^3 \to S^2$ & $U(1)$ phase \\
Bell (two-qubit) & $\mathbb{H}$ & $S^7 \to S^4$ & $SU(2)$ weak isospin \\
GHZ (special) & $\mathbb{O}$, $\mathbb{C}^3$ sector & $S^{15} \to S^8$ & $SU(3)$ colour / quarks (confined) \\
W (anti-special) & $\mathbb{O}$, $\mathbb{C}$ sector & $S^{15} \to S^8$ & colour singlets / leptons (free) \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The two octonionic rows share the same fibration and are separated only by their position relative
to the computability split: GHZ confined to $\mathbb{C}^3$, W reaching $\mathbb{C}$. That the
colour-triplet sector sits on the short-root coset of $G_2$, with the gluons on the long roots,
is the bridge to the mass discussion of \S\ref{sec:masses}, where the non-associativity of the
short-root directions is what distinguishes quark from lepton couplings.

\subsection{Relation to Szangolies's construction}
\label{sec:entanglement-szangolies}

It is worth being precise about the overlap, because the convergence is itself evidence. Szangolies
\autocite{szangolies2025standardmodel} obtains the same lepton/quark split directly from the
representation theory of the $\mathrm{Spin}(9)$ stabiliser: under the embedding of $U(1)\times SU(3)$
he finds the octonionic spinor decomposing into a leptonic part from the $\mathbb{C}$ factor --- an
$SU(3)$ singlet of hypercharge $-1$ --- and a quark part from $\mathbb{C}^3$ --- an $SU(3)$ triplet of
hypercharge $\tfrac13$ --- both transforming as $SU(2)$ doublets, that is, one left-handed generation.
This is reached with no reference to entanglement classes; the octonionic state is treated as
carrying a generation wholesale, and the split is a fact about the gauge group acting on
$\mathbb{C} \oplus \mathbb{C}^3$.

Our result is complementary rather than competing. Where Szangolies fixes the representation content
of each summand, Propositions~\ref{prop:ghz} and~\ref{prop:w-access} fix \emph{which states populate
which summand}, and do so by their SLOCC class: a genuinely tripartite GHZ-class state cannot leave
$\mathbb{C}^3$, and a W-class state generically reaches $\mathbb{C}$. The lepton/quark division he
assigns by representation theory we obtain as a consequence of entanglement type. The two arrivals
reinforce each other --- he reaches the assignment from the gauge side, we reach it from the
entanglement side --- and his independent derivation is the strongest external check we have that the
$\mathbb{C}$/$\mathbb{C}^3$ identification is not an artefact of our route. We adopt his
representation-theoretic assignment and supply the selection principle his construction does not
contain.

\subsection{What is proved and what is owed}

Proved here, or in the companion derivations carried into Paper~2: GHZ confinement to $\mathbb{C}^3$
(Proposition~\ref{prop:ghz}), W accessibility of $\mathbb{C}$ (Proposition~\ref{prop:w-access}), the
$SU(2)_L$ doublet content of W (Proposition~\ref{prop:w-doublet}), the topological character of
confinement, and $\theta_{\mathrm{QCD}} = 0$. These rest only on the composition-algebra identity and
the local-unitary invariance of single-qubit reduced spectra, with no free parameters and numerical
agreement to machine precision.

Owed, and flagged as such: the appearance of exactly three generations, which requires the triality
of the octonionic fibration together with the $K_3$ non-two-colourability obstruction
(\S\ref{sec:generations}); the orientation that fixes the $\mathbf{3}$ versus $\bar{\mathbf{3}}$
assignment of quark against antiquark, which the present pointwise statement does not determine; the
selection of $SU(2)_L$ over $SU(2)_R$ as physical weak isospin, structural but not yet a theorem; the
dynamical content of confinement, namely the string tension, which would require the torsionful Dirac
spectrum on the parallelised $S^7$ and remains open; and the quark--lepton mass ratios, which the
short-root/long-root split makes available but does not by itself fix (\S\ref{sec:masses}). The
division of fermions into quarks and leptons, however, is settled: it is the division of genuinely
tripartite entanglement into its two SLOCC classes.
